          "title": "Grobhausern",
          "subtitle": "Vying",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Grobhausern is a historical German vying game where players bet and compare four-card combinations from a 32-card pack."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Grobhausern, also called Grobhaus, is an historical German vying game. Players stake on four-card combinations using a 32-card piquet-style pack."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2-8 players use the table arrangement described for Grobhausern."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "32-card French or German-suited pack"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "32-card French or German-suited pack, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal four-card hands from the 32-card pack, then conduct betting and comparison."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
